1hc|n|Affection; inclination; passion; feeling; disposition.	N:3tn,11,3~3tn,11,3
1hc|v|To act upon; to produce an effect or change upon. ; To influence or move, as the feelings or passions; to touch. ; To love; to regard with affection. ; To show a fondness for; to like to use or practice; to choose; hence, to frequent habitually. ; To dispose or incline. ; To aim at; to aspire; to covet. ; To tend to by affinity or disposition. ; To make a show of; to put on a pretense of; to feign; to assume; as, to affect ignorance. ; To assign; to appoint.	o:1bdt,71,24;136,32,5;3tn,23,7;w95,16,3;1mx4,3,10;1mxc,2,5~1bdt,71,24;1mx4,3,10;3tn,23,7;136,32,5;1mxc,2,5;w95,16,3	s:1vf8,23,8~1vf8,23,8	d:1ca,91,3;1d7y,87,19;2032,46,8;1w8b,37,3;iub,33,6;bvt,24,4;2eq,9,15~1d7y,87,19;2eq,9,15;2032,46,8;iub,33,6;bvt,24,4;1ca,91,3;1w8b,37,3
